{
  "dom_id": "step-q45464",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "The point $P(-5,-2)$ is rotated ${270}^{∘}$ counterclockwise about the origin $O$ and then translated according to the function $(x,y)↦(x+p,y+q).$ If the image of $P$ under this sequence of transformations is $(2,-9),$ then $p+q=$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformations.\n\nA rotation of ${270}^{∘}$ counterclockwise about $O$ can be represented by \n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(y,-x).\n$$\n\nApplying this to the point $P,$ we get\n\n$$\n(-5,-2)↦(-2,5).\n$$\n\nNow, applying the translation to $(-2,5),$ we get\n\n$$\n(-2,5)↦(-2+p,5+q).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the resulting point is $(2,-9),$ by equating the $x$- and $y$-coordinates, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-2+p=2 \\\\ 5+q=-9\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}p=4 \\\\ q=-14.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\np-q=4+(-14)=-10.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
